  "slug": "concurrence-graph-spectra-d812",
  "summary": "New preprints pair quantum hardware encodings of gauge, light-matter and QCD cascades with improved classical solvers for spin, fermion and open-system dynamics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is simulation of real-time many-body dynamics, split between quantum-hardware encodings and classical methods. On the quantum side, a cold-atom analog simulator of a 1D SU(2) quantum link model observes coherent meson-baryon conversion under tunable mass and gauge parameters. A Trotterized hybrid qubit-boson circuit evolves the Jaynes-Cummings-Hubbard model and is benchmarked against exact diagonalization. A coherent quantum-circuit encoding of finite-state Mueller dipole branching at small x is compared with continuous cascades and H1 DIS data. On the classical side, cluster spin-LSC treats a sensor and strongly coupled bath spins quantum mechanically to model spin-qubit decoherence. Dirac propagation simulates local fermionic observables under particle-number-conserving unitaries. Transition path sampling is formulated for non-Markovian quantum state diffusion to extract rare-event rates. Separately, quantum Monte Carlo of 2D dipolar excitons yields an analytical framework for chemical potential and interaction energies.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
